# SYNTHETIC. Written from RFC 5321 section 4.2.1. Not a recording: phase-0 capture
# against a real server has not happened yet.
#
# 421 is "service not available, closing transmission channel", and it is what servers return
# when rate-limiting. It must map to Throttled, which backs off, and NOT to a refusal — a
# refusal is fatal, and the store answers fatal by applying the undo patch and dropping the
# outbox entry, which would discard the user's outgoing message.

S: 220 smtp.example ESMTP
C: EHLO client.example
S: 250-smtp.example Hello
S: 250-SIZE 35882577
S: 250-AUTH PLAIN LOGIN XOAUTH2
S: 250 PIPELINING
C: AUTH PLAIN AGFkYUBleGFtcGxlLmNvbQBzM2NyM3QtcGFzc3dvcmQ=
S: 235 2.7.0 Authentication successful
C: MAIL FROM:<ada@example.com>
S: 421 4.7.0 Too many messages, slow down
FAIL Throttled
